Subject: [PATCH 02233/11362] [conductor] In-process docs for PHASE D1 (ARC
 north star; UNSTALL the exp4307 harness failure) -- monotonic ARC +1 on a NEW
 game (total_levels >= 23) with a FRONTIER-ADAPTER-FREE solver. .398 (exp4307)
 STALLED at 22 and was FLAGGED GATE_PASSED_WITHOUT_DATA: it selected a game
 but exploration_actions_used=0 and real_env_confirmed=false because the
 frontier adapter was unavailable -- a HARNESS failure, not a science failure.
 .399 removes the adapter dependency: use the TRAINING-FREE GRAPH-EXPLORE
 solver (arXiv:2512.24156 -- segment frames into components, prioritize
 actions by visual salience, maintain a directed state-transition graph, take
 the shortest path to an untested state-action pair; median 30/52 levels with
 NO learning) so the solve does NOT depend on an unavailable adapter. Target
 the best-headroom UNATTEMPTED game from the 25-game survey (NOT
 r11l/ls20/wa30/sc25). HARD anti-flag gate (the exp4307 flag must NOT recur):
 exploration_actions_used>0 AND real_env_confirmed=true AND
 offline_reproduced=true (per ARC Solve Reproducibility Discipline -- only
 offline-reproduced levels count). Advance ONE game by >=1 NEW
 real-env-confirmed level (total 22 -> >=23). Report total_levels +
 game_advanced + levels_completed + exploration_actions_used +
 offline_reproduced. NO TRM training; NO leaderboard submission. An honest
 no-advance WITH exploration_actions_used>0 is COMPLETE and informs the next
 game pick (a no-advance with 0 actions is the flag to avoid).

